#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d44d3c77-9dba-598d-954b-911825fd5ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293237} {:answer/id #uuid "0070ead1-e2f0-5ce4-852e-e97f98880a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293238} {:answer/id #uuid "dd527b83-3fb6-5fd7-b3dd-d9fdd02c0f6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293239} {:answer/id #uuid "438af1d9-cd06-5296-bc6b-aace32f7ce92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293240} {:answer/id #uuid "134c774d-efad-5307-a595-fe47c70bf6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d44d3c77-9dba-598d-954b-911825fd5ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293237} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f485e2d-8f17-5aeb-b725-490810dd4d8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fbccf84-6c3c-5304-8aee-294db81f5c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-49682" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & +2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =2[-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]+2[0-0] \\\\  & =2(-2\\pi )+0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
